    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d275">

                <pb facs="0395" n="[395]" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg395"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Angel to Mr. Seward</hi>.</head>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">[Extract.]</note>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 76.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the
                            United States</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Stockholm</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-05-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 22, 1861</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>The Swedish law is very strict against the violation of the rights of neutrals,
                    and I am assured that there is no apprehension that any of the ports of this
                    kingdom or of Norway will he prostituted to the wicked purpose of fitting out
                    privateers.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with much respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>B. F. ANGEL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
